# Authentication Settings (ADR-002, design 18.6, issue GH-145)
#
# Leave every VITE_ENTRA_* value blank for local Development: the app runs as an unauthenticated
# pass-through shell (no MSAL, no Entra sign-in) -- the backend enforces Production separately.
#
# For an explicit Entra deployment, set VITE_AUTH_MODE=Entra plus a real, non-placeholder tenant id
# and client id (both fail the build via `npm run prebuild` / `validate:auth-config` if only one is
# set, or if the value looks like a placeholder). VITE_ENTRA_API_SCOPE defaults to
# "access_as_user" (requested as api://{VITE_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID}/{scope}) and rarely needs to change.
#
# VITE_AUTH_MODE=Entra
VITE_ENTRA_TENANT_ID=
VITE_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_ENTRA_API_SCOPE=access_as_user
